    "title": "Former Cheatham County Sheriff's Office K-9 Loretta dead at 13 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Pat O&#8217;Donnell ,\n6 hours ago\nCHEATHAM COUNTY, Tenn. (WKRN) — The Cheatham County Sheriff’s Office is celebrating the life of K-9 Loretta.\nLoretta died on Tuesday. She was 13 years old.\n⏩ Read today’s top stories on wkrn.com\nIn December 2024, Loretta retired after a 10-year career with the sheriff’s office where she served as a narcotics dog. She was deployed 179 times and sniffed out 490 pounds of illegal drugs.\n(Photo: Jacob Kent) (Photo: Jacob Kent) (Photo: Cheatham County Sheriff’s Office) Her longtime handler was Cheatham County deputy Jacob Kent.\n📧 Have breaking news come to you: Subscribe to News 2 email alerts →\nLoretta assisted several agencies across Middle Tennessee including the Montgomery County Sheriff’s Office, whose K-9 team paid respects to Loretta on Tuesday.\nLoretta was recently failing in health and died on Tuesday. She will be cremated.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRN News 2.",
    "summary": "⏩ Read today’s top stories on wkrn.com In December 2024, Loretta retired after a 10-year career with the sheriff’s office where she served as a narcotics dog. She was deployed 179 times and sniffed out 490 pounds of illegal drugs. (Photo: Jacob Kent) (Photo: Jacob Kent) (Photo: Cheatham County Sheriff’s Office) Her longtime handler was Cheatham County deputy Jacob Kent. 📧 Have breaking news come to you: Subscribe to News 2 email alerts → Loretta assisted several agencies across Middle Tennessee including the Montgomery County Sheriff’s Office, whose K-9 team paid respects to Loretta on Tuesday.",
